# Tests that cannot apply on Windows, one per line: file::test | reason. Read by tests/lib.sh; each is reported as SKIPPED with its reason.
test_doctor::test_a_hook_command_that_is_missing_or_not_executable_is_a_problem | NTFS has no executable bit, chmod -x changes nothing
test_doctor::test_doctor_checks_the_timer_only_when_the_state_says_one_is_installed | installs a systemd timer, Windows has none
test_doctor_repos::test_a_repository_whose_config_hangs_git_becomes_a_timed_out_finding_instead_of_a_hang | needs a FIFO, which Git for Windows cannot create for native git
test_doctor_repos::test_a_timed_out_doctor_run_leaves_no_process_behind | needs ps -x and process groups
test_doctor_repos::test_an_unreadable_directory_is_a_listed_problem_and_the_rest_is_still_checked | NTFS ignores chmod, so nothing is unreadable
